* MathFn1 component reference -- the "## Example" netlist verbatim.
* No title line -- see doc-verify/const/example.cir's own comment for why.
*
* T -> G (gain k = 2*pi*1000) -> S builds sin(2*pi*1000*t) out of ordinary blocks; C and E show
* two more MathFn1 functions applied to the same sources. SQ shows the Vector rule: a Vector
* input is mapped elementwise (sqrt of [1,4,9] is [1,2,3]). See
* test_mathfn.py::test_example_fn1_scalar_functions_and_elementwise_vector.
T kind=time
G kind=gain in=T k=6283.185307179586
S kind=sin in=G
C kind=cos in=G
E kind=exp in=T
SV kind=const value=[1,4,9]
SQ kind=sqrt in=SV
